  Phase 1 Run & Test Steps
  
  Phase 1 is the Foundation Setup — it validates the Docker Compose stack, database,
   and base infrastructure come up cleanly.

  Step 1: Create your .env file

  cp .env.example .env

  Then edit .env and fill in the required values:

  ┌────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  What to set: agentic-infraops (matches your credentials)
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Variable: GCP_SA_KEY_PATH
  What to set: ./secrets/gcp-sa.json (already exists)
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Variable: GMAIL_CREDENTIALS_PATH
  What to set: ./secrets/gmail-credentials.json (already exists)
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Variable: OPENAI_API_KEY or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
  What to set: Your LLM provider key
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Variable: LITELLM_MASTER_KEY
  What to set: Any string, e.g. sk-local-dev
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Variable: AIRFLOW_FERNET_KEY
  What to set: Generate with: python -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; 
    print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"
  ────────────────────────────────────────
  Variable: All changeme passwords
  What to set: Set to anything for local dev

  Step 2: Start the stack

  docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml up -d
docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml --env-file .env up -d 
  This starts PostgreSQL, Qdrant, PubSub emulator, LiteLLM, Airflow, Prometheus,
  Grafana, and all MCP servers.

  Step 3: Wait for services to be healthy, then run DB migrations

  # Check all containers are running
  docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml --env-file .env ps

  # Run migrations
  python infrastructure/scripts/migrate.py --env local

  Step 4: Seed the knowledge base

  python infrastructure/scripts/seed_knowledge_base.py \
    --docs-dir docs/knowledge/ \
    --qdrant-url http://localhost:6333


